 I  will see what the candidates are saying  about how they want to represent us what  their views on issues are I have to say  the response from my local community has  been fantastic and the support I've had  over the past few days has been amazing  people of email me stopped me in the  street to say that they feel I'm doing  my job as an MP so you're not you're  you're not sure if you're going to vote  conservative or the next election then  you might vote for someone else I remain  a member I remain a member of the  Conservative Party but I think at the  end of the day I'm like every voter I  will try and work through what I feel  the right thing is for my  community in my country and then cast my  vote accordingly and I really would urge  the Conservative Party to consider how  it can make sure it can continue to  reach out to communities like my own and  I think we are we are owed a proper  choice in this election and I am worried  that Britain faces a lose-lose choice  either a No Deal Boris Johnson  government or a hard left Marxist  effectively Corbin government I don't  think that's the kind of choice that the  British people deserve I think they  deserve something much much better than  that and I hope that in the end Britain  will work its way through this broke  trick gridlock and then we have to at  some point get on to what I feel is the  big issue facing Britain which is  inequality of opportunity and all I can  say is that I don't plan to leave  frontline politics I plan to put my time  into fixing what I think the real  challenge is for Britain which is an  equality of opportunity and that  whenever Britain is able to get onto  that real debate I will be at the front  of that debate leading the charge and  hopefully making a difference on the  ground in the meantime I'm it just  finally I'm came to know what happened  when the news was broken that you'd be  stripped to the conservative whip I mean  who spanked you how do they get in touch  well I was travelling home on the  district line I don't normally do and I  had a call from the chief where privacy  wasn't able to take it on the tube so he  simply left a voicemail and what did I  say just informed me that the wit was  being withdrawn I think it might have  been polite after 14 years to try to  call me back perhaps a second time but  the bottom line Sofie is that I think we  are where we are and I I'm very clear  what my role is and my role is to  represent my community in Parliament and  that's what I did that day so did you  have any conversations after that  because Boris Johnson tried to get in  touch with you and they Dominic Cummings  nobody else has called you about to  called you about call  no just the voicemail just a voicemail  and how does that make you feel what  look I think it says an awful lot more  about I guess the state is a  Conservative Party  and it does about me and and I think in  a way I have served my community in my  country for 14 years and I think it's a  shame that the whip has been withdrawn  for me doing the simple thing of  representing my community in Parliament  I'm not in control of how the  conservative leadership takes its  decisions I think it was a  self-defeating move to withdraw the whip  and I think it will backfire but  ultimately those are questions for  Dominic Cummings and Boris Johnson more  than they are for me

